{
    "version": "1.9.20",
    "changelog": "A small self-delivered fix, from Joshua's first hands-on with 1.9.19. (1) THE TOOLBAR ICONS ARE IN COLOUR NOW: the 1.9.19 pictograms were thin line drawings in one near-black ink, and on the toolbar's gray they read as a row of black smudges \u2014 'very hard to find out what's what.' Every tool is redrawn in its own saturated colour with a bold filled silhouette that reads at the toolbar's real 24x24 size: Zone is green land with yellow pins, Delete a red trash can, Draw a blue pencil, Merge teal and sky strands becoming one road, Detail Edit a cyan magnifier, and so on \u2014 neighbouring buttons are far apart in hue, so the row scans by colour alone. The old check only proved the pictures were non-blank; the new gate measures dominant hue per icon, hue separation between neighbours, and the near-black share. Two tooltips also name their tool properly now (Extend, Find Stacked). (2) THE REFERENCE PANE SAYS WHAT IT IS: the Resource and Reference pane draws the read-only source map by design, so roads deleted from the game still show there \u2014 with nothing saying so, it read as a bug. A plain line under the layer buttons now reads: 'Reference (source map) \u2014 deletions in the game don't remove these lines'. Nothing else changes: this payload arrives by itself \u2014 the editor staged it in the background and the launcher runs it on the next start, exactly as 1.9.19 promised.",
